  "party_positions": [
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Dreeben",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "c25a732096714a4fc0fc7db2225f67e7426ab35201261b3d1d971f711b6da5ed",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-c25a73209671-0002-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 39,
                "start": 39
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "Mr. Dreeben argued that the petitioner\u2019s position is consistent with reading statutes both for what they say and for what they mean."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Dreeben",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "c25a732096714a4fc0fc7db2225f67e7426ab35201261b3d1d971f711b6da5ed",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-c25a73209671-0002-0004"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 42,
                "start": 42
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Dreeben, mr. Dreeben said he is not aware that Congress has legislated in this area after *Booker*."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Dreeben",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "c25a732096714a4fc0fc7db2225f67e7426ab35201261b3d1d971f711b6da5ed",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-c25a73209671-0002-0006"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 44,
                "start": 44
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Dreeben, mr. Dreeben described the sentencing scheme as being done in a logically proportional manner."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Nachmanoff",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "c25a732096714a4fc0fc7db2225f67e7426ab35201261b3d1d971f711b6da5ed",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-c25a73209671-0002-0009"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 49,
                "start": 49
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Nachmanoff, mr. Nachmanoff noted that roughly 70\u202fpercent of crack sentences are imposed at the mandatory minimum or just above it."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Petitioner (Derrick Kimbrough)",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Government",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "c25a732096714a4fc0fc7db2225f67e7426ab35201261b3d1d971f711b6da5ed",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-c25a73209671-0001-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 20,
                "start": 20
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "The Government contended that 18\u202fU.S.C.\u202f\u00a7\u202f3553(a) requires individualized sentencing and that judges must follow its mandates and calculate the advisory Guidelines correctly in every case."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Respondent",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "c25a732096714a4fc0fc7db2225f67e7426ab35201261b3d1d971f711b6da5ed",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-c25a73209671-0001-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 23,
                "start": 23
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Respondent, the United States asked whether a district court can reasonably disagree with Congress concerning the ratio between quantity\u2011based sentences for crack and powder cocaine."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Respondent (United States)",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    }
